Package: clinthresh
Title: Clinical Thresholds, Equivalence Tests and Replicability Tools for Sports Medicine Research
Version: 0.1.7
Authors@R: person("Zacharias", "Papadakis", email = "zach.papadakis@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8437-8067"))
Description: Tools to read and design sports medicine and rehabilitation studies
    against thresholds of clinical importance rather than against zero. Runs
    equivalence tests (two one-sided tests) from published estimates and
    confidence intervals, classifies intervals as clinically important,
    trivial, equivalent or inconclusive, computes the smallest worthwhile
    change, standard error of measurement and minimal detectable change,
    the small-telescopes bound for replications, and sample sizes for
    equivalence and non-inferiority trials. Ships a sourced reference table of
    minimal important differences and an interactive web app.
